      "writtenOn": "2025-11-03T16:19:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Question for @cwallez@chromium.org: I\u0027m doing this \"End/Start\" thing here, which works, but misses capturing the very first frame. My initial thought was to hook into `SharedTextureMemory::BeginAccessImpl` for the `StartFrameCapture`, and `SharedTextureMemory::EndAccessImpl` (what\u0027s currently calling `NotifySwapChainPresent`) for the `EndFrameCapture`, but I wasn\u0027t sure if these Begin/EndAccessImpl calls are really called at the start and end of the frame so that all D3D12 commands in between are properly captured.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 460,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 461,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "a4081b5c572418367c9876d94c942e5e0f16a261",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8dcf622b_d5810b13",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/d3d12/TextureD3D12.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 461,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000014
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-03T20:07:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m pretty sure BeginAccessImpl can happen later in the frame. E.g. in the requestAnimationFrame callback in JS you can do a bunch of stuff before calling getCurrentTexture(), that should be considered part of the frame.\n\nYou could put a StartFrameCapture in device creation maybe? Would that be bad if it turns out to be a device that never presents anything?",
      "parentUuid": "9bef964e_714c0054",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 460,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 461,
        "endChar": 71
      },
      "revId": "a4081b5c572418367c9876d94c942e5e0f16a261",
